; claude: the pieces of a window that the browser's chrome is made of
; but that know nothing of a browser: text in fixed cells and the
; status bubble (Gui_text), a menu opened at a point (Gui_menu), the
; strip of tabs (Gui_tabs), a row of picture buttons (Gui_toolbar);
; their colours and their style (Gui_kit). Geometry and shapes; what a
; hit means, and when a menu opens, is the program's.
;
; Not tiny_libs' gui (Widget, Immediate, Mvu, ...), whose widgets read
; the mouse as a record a frame and keep their own state: these are
; values a Model-View-Update program keeps in its model and draws in
; its view. Their modules are Gui_, that library's being linked too
; (libs/richtext) and the Playground's own being Gui.
(library
 (name mini_gui)
 (wrapped false)
 (libraries
   elm_playground ; the shapes
   tiny_libs.gui)) ; Text.chars, a string's characters
